WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.199
One project. Every machine.
Shared repositories bring Studio and Laptop terminals into one map.

2
00:00:05.199 --> 00:00:10.483
Know where attention is needed
Blue is working. Green is done. Red is waiting for your input.

3
00:00:10.483 --> 00:00:16.235
Follow the hand-off
Select a terminal to inspect its directed communication and delegation.

4
00:00:16.235 --> 00:00:30.010
See progress as it changes
Demo status updates: waiting for input, then working, then done.

5
00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:38.183
Keep machine context
Machine clouds group terminals while repositories remain shared.

6
00:00:38.183 --> 00:00:46.293
Zoom out to the project flow
Hide terminals. Directed relationships roll up to repositories.

7
00:00:46.293 --> 00:00:53.736
Keep the legend in view
The filters stay visible in one compact row. Restore terminals with one click.

8
00:00:53.736 --> 00:01:01.884
Find the terminal you need
Search keeps its shared repository context and exact checkout details.

9
00:01:01.884 --> 00:01:10.581
A clear view of the whole herd
Three repositories. Two PCs. One place to see work and relationships.
